KG42.register("rules-107069e4dd4c27979a6fcd13",{"id":"02-dlmp::v141-c-R006","paper":"02-dlmp","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"Constrained social-welfare optimization of the electric distribution system determines the next-day DLMPs. Scope: Next-day DLMP formation in the local DSO market. Condition: EV aggregators are modeled as price takers and demand price elasticity is included. The DSO calculates DLMPs using forecast demand and accounting for the electric distribution network topology. Scope: Distribution-network DLMP calculation in the proposed DSO procedure. The DLMP equals the reference LMP plus the locational congestion markup. Scope: DLMP price decomposition under the RBTS simplification. Condition: The generation-node PTDF coefficient is set to zero and conventional household demand has an interior solution with respect to its non-negativity constraint.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.social_welfare","coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E002","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E37"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"DLMP price decomposition under the RBTS simplification. | Distribution-network DLMP calculation in the proposed DSO procedure. | Next-day DLMP formation in the local DSO market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E37"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x_P_DLMP","symbol":"P_{DLMP,i,t}","meaning":"Distribution locational marginal price at time period t at node i of the distribution grid; the endogenous local price produced by the DSO clearing and used in the DLMP decomposition.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued price (source gives no explicit sign restriction)","unit":null,"indices":["i in N_c","t in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22"]},{"variable_id":"x_varphi","symbol":"\\varphi_{i,t}","meaning":"Locational congestion markup at time period t at node i, defined as the sum over lines of the difference between positive and negative line-flow duals weighted by the line-to-node PTDF coefficient.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued congestion markup (defined as a linear combination of line duals and PTDFs; no explicit sign restriction in source)","unit":null,"indices":["i in N_c","t in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22"]},{"variable_id":"x_lambda_plus","symbol":"\\lambda^+_{l,t}","meaning":"Dual variable for the positive line-flow constraint of line l at time period t; shadow price of the upper line-flow limit.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real (dual feasibility/complementarity condition (22)/(23))","unit":null,"indices":["l in L","t in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E22"]},{"variable_id":"x_lambda_minus","symbol":"\\lambda^-_{l,t}","meaning":"Dual variable for the negative line-flow constraint of line l at time period t; shadow price of the lower line-flow limit.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real (dual feasibility/complementarity condition (22)/(23))","unit":null,"indices":["l in L","t in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E22"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_P_LMP","symbol":"P_{LMP,t}","meaning":"System locational marginal price at time period t for the node feeding the distribution grid; treated as the reference price input in the DLMP decomposition.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"system LMP at time period t for the node feeding the distribution grid; reference price input to the DLMP decomposition"},"unit":null,"indices":["t in T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22"]},{"parameter_id":"theta_D_li","symbol":"D_{l,i}","meaning":"Power transfer distribution factor (PTDF) coefficient of line l with respect to a unit injection at node i; in the DLMP decomposition it is evaluated at the demand node i and weights the congestion dual difference.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"network PTDF parameter from the distribution topology"},"unit":null,"indices":["l in L","i in N_c"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Constrained social-welfare optimization of the electric distribution system determines the next-day DLMPs. Scope: Next-day DLMP formation in the local DSO market. Condition: EV aggregators are modeled as price takers and demand price elasticity is included.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E14"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DSO calculates DLMPs using forecast demand and accounting for the electric distribution network topology. Scope: Distribution-network DLMP calculation in the proposed DSO procedure.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E37"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The DLMP equals the reference LMP plus the locational congestion markup. Scope: DLMP price decomposition under the RBTS simplification. Condition: The generation-node PTDF coefficient is set to zero and conventional household demand has an interior solution with respect to its non-negativity constraint.","expression":"P_{DLMP,i,t} = P_{LMP,t} + \\varphi_{i,t}   (33)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_P_DLMP","x_varphi"],"parameter_refs":["theta_P_LMP"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The locational congestion markup \\varphi_{i,t} equals the sum over lines of the difference between the positive and negative line-flow dual variables weighted by the line-to-node PTDF coefficient D_{l,i}. Scope: DLMP price decomposition under the RBTS simplification.","expression":"\\varphi_{i,t} = \\sum_{l \\in L}(\\lambda^+_{l,t} - \\lambda^-_{l,t}) D_{l,i}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_varphi","x_lambda_plus","x_lambda_minus"],"parameter_refs":["theta_D_li"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":"203","section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"Abstract This paper presents an integrated distribution lo cational marginal pricing (DLMP) method d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In the proposed approach, the distribution system operator (DSO) determines distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) by solving the social welfare optimization of the electric distribution system which considers EV aggregators as price takers in the local DSO market and demand price elasticity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E08","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":"204","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"and PowerWorld [19]. ere The DCOPF was adopted in the derivation of DLMPs as a to practical approach","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The DCOPF was adopted in the derivation of DLMPs as a practical approach to address the computational complexity resulting from the large number of nodes within the electric distribution network. In the proposed DLMP algorithm, the DSO determines the DLMPs for the next day by solving a constrained social welfare maximization problem."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"205","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"( ) beneﬁt of the EV demand is not included in the objective func- tion since that component is cons","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The objective function consists of two components, social value of meeting the conventional demand, given by the area under the demand functions, and the cost of satisfying both the EV demand and the conventional demand, as shown in (1). The benefit of the EV demand is not included in the objective function since that component is constant, as long as the EV demand is met within the day, and is not affected by the charging schedule. Instead, a constraint requiring that the EV demand be met by the schedule is included. To be more specific, the object function in (1) can be further decomposed into three terms as shown by"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"206","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"(29) In the RBTS, the power transfer distribution factor (PTDF) coefﬁcient associated with the gener","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the RBTS, the power transfer distribution factor (PTDF) coefficient associated with the generation node D_{l,g} is set to be 0 to enable unlimited import from the grid to the distribution network, which simplifies (29) and yields\n\\rho_{i,t} = P_{LMP,t} + \\sum_{l \\in L}(\\lambda^+_{l,t} - \\lambda^-_{l,t}) D_{l,i}   (30)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"206","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"( ) ch (32) gr th ch The non-negativity constraint (7) can be excluded by implic- itly assuming an i","equation_id":"(33)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The non-negativity constraint (7) can be excluded by implicitly assuming an interior solution with respect to these constraints, forcing the dual variable associated with the constraint \\xi_{i,t} = 0. This can be explained as: every conventional household consumes at least a small positive amount of energy. Under this assumption, the DLMPs become\nP_{DLMP,i,t} = P_{LMP,t} + \\varphi_{i,t}   (33)\nwhere \\varphi_{i,t} = \\sum_{l \\in L}(\\lambda^+_{l,t} - \\lambda^-_{l,t}) D_{l,i}. The DLMPs can be interpreted as the sum of the reference price P_{LMP,t} and the locational congestion markup \\varphi_{i,t}, which is analogous to the marginal cost of congestion in the LMPs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E37","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"207","section":"IV. Alleviating Congestion From EVs Within Electric Distribution Networks Using DLMP","anchor_text":"caused by the EV charging demand. The congestion alleviation 2) approach using DLMP is illustrated i","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The DSO plays a major role in the DLMP-based congestion management within electric distribution networks. The concept can be explained by the following steps.\nStep 1) The DSO obtains the LMPs from the posted day-ahead energy prices.\nStep 2) According to the EV data within the electric distribution network, the expected EV demand will be forecasted by the DSO with the assumption that all EV aggregators are minimizing their EV charging costs. Conventional demand will be forecasted by the DSO according to the posted energy prices.\nStep 3) With the information on the forecasted demand, the DSO calculates the DLMPs at the electric distribution network level taking into account the electric distribution network topology.\nStep 4) In the end, the DLMPs will be sent to all EV aggregators and retailers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":"205","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"(22) nc- de- ng (23) be ect as (24) (25) (26) (27) (28)","equation_id":"(22)-(28)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"(22) \\lambda^-_{l,t} \\ge 0 \\perp \\sum_{i \\in N} D_{l,i} r_{i,t} + K_l \\ge 0 \\;\\; \\forall l \\in L, \\forall t \\in T\n(23) \\lambda^+_{l,t} \\ge 0 \\perp K_l - \\sum_{i \\in N} D_{l,i} r_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\;\\; \\forall l \\in L, \\forall t \\in T\n(24) \\xi_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\perp c_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\;\\; \\forall i \\in N_c, \\forall t \\in T\n(25) \\mu^-_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\perp x_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\;\\; \\forall i \\in N_c, \\forall t \\in T\n(26) \\mu^+_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\perp E_{i,t} - x_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\;\\; \\forall i \\in N_c, \\forall t \\in T\n(27) \\kappa^-_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\perp S_{i,0} + \\sum_{t' \\le t-1} x_{i,t'} - \\sum_{t' \\le t} d_{i,t'} - S^-_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\;\\; \\forall i \\in N_c, \\forall t \\in T \\backslash \\{1\\}\n(28) \\kappa^+_{i,t} \\ge 0 \\perp S^+_{i,t} - S_{i,0} - \\sum_{t' \\le t-1} x_{i,t'} + \\sum_{t' \\le t} d_{i,t'} \\ge 0 \\;\\; \\forall i \\in N_c, \\forall t \\in T \\backslash \\{1\\}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"206","section":"II. Determination of DLMPs Using Integrated Optimization","anchor_text":"(29) In the RBTS, the power transfer distribution factor (PTDF) coefﬁcient associated with the gener","equation_id":"(31)-(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The DLMPs can be derived by combining (11) and (30) to yield\n(31) P_{DLMP,i,t} = P_{i,t}(c_{i,t}) = \\rho_{i,t} - \\xi_{i,t}\n(32) \\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\; = P_{LMP,t} + \\sum_{l \\in L}(\\lambda^+_{l,t} - \\lambda^-_{l,t}) D_{l,i} - \\xi_{i,t}"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","quote":"In the proposed approach, the distribution system operator (DSO) determines distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) by solving the social welfare optimization of the electric distribution system which considers EV aggregators as price takers in the local DSO market and demand price elasticity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E08","quote":"In the proposed DLMP algorithm, the DSO determines the DLMPs for the next day by solving a constrained social welfare maximization problem."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","quote":"The objective function consists of two components, social value of meeting the conventional demand, given by the area under the demand functions, and the cost of satisfying both the EV demand and the conventional demand, as shown in (1)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E37","quote":"With the information on the forecasted demand, the DSO calculates the DLMPs at the electric distribution network level taking into account the electric distribution network topology."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E20","quote":"In the RBTS, the power transfer distribution factor (PTDF) coefficient associated with the generation node D_{l,g} is set to be 0 to enable unlimited import from the grid to the distribution network"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","quote":"The non-negativity constraint (7) can be excluded by implicitly assuming an interior solution with respect to these constraints"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","quote":"The DLMPs can be interpreted as the sum of the reference price P_{LMP,t} and the locational congestion markup \\varphi_{i,t}, which is analogous to the marginal cost of congestion in the LMPs."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"8aa994a7892c818f0ff99fd31e35214ecf44110cc46b249c15033f49d8ccff27","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The rule's pricing content is formalized from the source-supported DLMP decomposition: C003 is transcribed as (33) P_{DLMP,i,t} = P_{LMP,t} + \\varphi_{i,t}, and supporting constraint C004 transcribes the source definition of the locational congestion markup \\varphi_{i,t} = \\sum_{l \\in L}(\\lambda^+_{l,t} - \\lambda^-_{l,t}) D_{l,i}. C001 and C002 remain procedural not_formalized because they state process requirements (DSO social-welfare optimization determines DLMPs; DSO calculates DLMPs using forecast demand and network topology) rather than a self-contained formula within this rule. B evidence is unreviewed candidate support; no independent B source audit, C.2 review or Agent E validation was performed. The frozen graph represents the pricing node and its two incoming relations, but the source's line-index set L and the full optimization variables/duals are not declared as graph objects, so full formalization of C001 would require C.1 revision.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the procedural requirement that constrained social-welfare clearing determines next-day DLMPs; graph edge E001 links clearing.social_welfare to pricing.local and carries C001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"C002 is the procedural requirement that the DSO calculates DLMPs with forecast demand and network topology; graph edge E002 links coordination.local_operator to pricing.local and carries C002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001","v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"The formalized DLMP decomposition is a price relationship at pricing.local; the DLMP is produced by the social-welfare clearing relation (E001) and is calculated by the local operator (E002)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C004","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001","v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"The congestion-markup definition is a component of the local DLMP; the markup arises from clearing duals (E001) and is computed as part of the DSO pricing procedure (E002)."},{"object_id":"x_P_DLMP","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001","v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"P_{DLMP,i,t} is the local price object at pricing.local; it is determined by the clearing relation E001 and calculated by the local operator relation E002."},{"object_id":"x_varphi","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001","v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"\\varphi_{i,t} is the locational congestion markup component of the DLMP at pricing.local; it derives from clearing duals via E001 and is part of the DSO pricing calculation E002."},{"object_id":"x_lambda_plus","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"\\lambda^+_{l,t} is a dual variable of the line-flow constraints in the social-welfare clearing problem at clearing.social_welfare; edge E001 links it into the local pricing relation."},{"object_id":"x_lambda_minus","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"\\lambda^-_{l,t} is a dual variable of the line-flow constraints in the social-welfare clearing problem at clearing.social_welfare; edge E001 links it into the local pricing relation."},{"object_id":"theta_P_LMP","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001","v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"P_{LMP,t} is the reference price component of the DLMP at pricing.local; it is an input to the pricing relation E001/E002."},{"object_id":"theta_D_li","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"D_{l,i} is a distribution-network topology parameter used by the DSO when calculating DLMPs; C002 and edge E002 capture the DSO calculation taking network topology into account."}],"revision_requests":["C.1 should add a graph/set object for L (the set of lines) because the source uses \\sum_{l \\in L} in the DLMP expressions (30)/(33), but L is not defined in the frozen NOMENCLATURE extraction (see v141-b-g01-E10, v141-b-g01-E16, v141-b-g01-E19 unresolved_refs).","For full formalization of C001 (constrained social-welfare optimization determining DLMPs), C.1 should declare or bind the optimization variables c_{i,t}, x_{i,t}, r_{i,t}, q_{g,t}, the dual variables \\xi, \\mu, \\kappa and index sets N_c, N_n, N_g, T with graph bindings; they are currently outside this rule's declared x/theta, so only the pricing decomposition C003/C004 is formalized.","B evidence used here is unreviewed and remains unverified; independent B source audit, C.2 independent review and Agent E were omitted in this experiment, so no claim is made that the transcription or downstream formalization has passed source review.","Source ambiguities that should be resolved by B re-extraction before extending formalization beyond C003/C004: equation (10) prints the same left expression on both sides; equations (34)/(36)/(37) show nonterminal-set notation as T\\{T} in some OCR regions versus T\\{|T|}; equations (45)-(46) overlap on \\mu^+_{i,t} \\ge 0."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
